{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ryghlW5IVVgjUfQ2BHo0dW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"11:223 Category · Bill & Utilities -> 11:300\n11:175 Credit Score Entry -> 10:235,11:466\nI11:311;7:22 Back -> 7:13,11:134\nI11:477;7:32 Back -> 7:13,11:134\n[{\"nodeId\":\"11:134\",\"name\":\"Budget · This Month\"}]\n7:2 Components · Budget | 11:134 01_Expenses | 11:300 02_Bill | 11:466 03_Credit_Score"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26d7c23f-3381-47cf-9fcd-bed7f7968ebf","uuid":"977a2794-6595-4701-aefb-c440976edc33","timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:02:08.698Z","tool_use_result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11:223 Category · Bill & Utilities -> 11:300\n11:175 Credit Score Entry -> 10:235,11:466\nI11:311;7:22 Back -> 7:13,11:134\nI11:477;7:32 Back -> 7:13,11:134\n[{\"nodeId\":\"11:134\",\"name\":\"Budget · This Month\"}]\n7:2 Components · Budget | 11:134 01_Expenses | 11:300 02_Bill | 11:466 03_Credit_Score"}],"_meta":{"mcpRequestId":"b0af5131-2918-461e-87e4-ccab431a0472"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01ryghlW5IVVgjUfQ2BHo0dW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vjo6akqt7fqfcad3vei7n6ceyefaynyey2mzcbcebtvwgw6dr7uv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_read_input_tokens":72910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":561,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26d7c23f-3381-47cf-9fcd-bed7f7968ebf","uuid":"f60cd185-0305-45c9-897d-aef5c4bff2b1","timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:02:21.292Z","thinking_duration_ms":7506}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vjo6akqt7fqfcad3vei7n6ceyefaynyey2mzcbcebtvwgw6dr7uv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three screens are built in 03 · Workspace, wired as a clickable prototype, and checked in screenshots. Before writing anything I confirmed the account was zuohaosheng@tetras.ai. I didn't touch the reference pages.\n\n**File:** https://www.figma.com/design/htzJEgTQZM6qy0UMgMs235/\n**03 · Workspace page ID:** `4:2`\n\n**Screens** (375 wide, light mode, DM Sans, brand color #6347EB):\n| Frame | ID | What's on it |\n|---|---|---|\n| `01_Expenses` | `11:134` | Header: back · \"Expenses\" · add. \"September 2020\" period picker, total spent $1,812, and a budget card with Left to spend $738, Monthly budget $2,550 and a 71% bar. A credit score card (660 · Good). Two category cards: Auto & transport $600 and Bill & Utilities $320, with all five item rows showing amount, amount left and a progress bar. A \"More categories\" row. The tab bar is fixed to the bottom with This Month selected. The frame is 1372 tall and scrolls vertically. |\n| `02_Bill` | `11:300` | Header: back · \"Bill\" · add. Bills / Payments / Subscription tabs, with Subscription selected. \"Your monthly payment for subscriptions\" $58.97. Four rows in the brief's order (Patreon membership, Netflix, Apple payment, Spotify), each with its logo, price and a right chevron. Tab bar. |\n| `03_Credit_Score` | `11:466` | Header: back · \"Credit Score\". A half-circle gauge showing 660 on the 400–850 range, with \"Good\", \"+6pts\" and \"Last update on 20 Jul 2020\". Three factor rows (On-time payments, Credit Utilization, Age of credit) with value, rating badge and detail. Tab bar. |\n\n**Prototype links:**\n- On 01, the Bill & Utilities card opens 02, sliding in from the right.\n- On 01, the credit score card opens 03. The brief gave no entry point, so I chose this card.\n- The back button on 02 and on 03 returns to 01.\n- Extra: tapping the This Month tab on 02 or 03 also returns to 01.\n- The prototype starts on 01 (\"Budget · This Month\").\n- Rows, tabs, segments, buttons and the period picker switch to a pressed look while you hold them down.\n\n**Design system:**\n- **Components** (frame `7:2`, \"Components · Budget\", next to the screens): icon button, header, tab item and tab bar, segment and segmented control, period picker, budget summary, progress row, category card, more-categories row, subscription summary, subscription row (logo can be swapped), credit score gauge, factor row and credit score card. Most have variants for the current, pressed, disabled and rating states.\n- **Tokens:** color variables, spacing and corner-radius variables, 10 text styles and 3 shadow styles.\n- **Reuse:** the screens are made entirely of instances of these components. The status bar and home indicator come from 02 · Components, and the icons and service logos from 04 · Media.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Age of credit has no detail value in the brief's data, so its detail line reads \"Average age of your accounts\".\n- I added some copy that isn't in the brief: \"Total spent\", \"Categories\", \"Budget · Spent\", \"2 items\" / \"3 items\", the \"47% used\"-style labels, \"See all categories\", \"4 active\", \"Subscriptions\", \"Score factors\", \"3 factors\" and the \"$1,812 spent · 71%\" / \"29% left\" line on the budget card. These are headings and figures calculated from the brief's numbers.\n- On 02, \"Patreon membership\" wraps onto two lines so it doesn't run into the price."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_read_input_tokens":72910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":561,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26d7c23f-338